comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T22:07:15.361Z","harness:codex","Progress evidence: the contract now declares replacement versus behavior_preserving semantics instead of inferring strength from prose. An executable temporary-tracker corpus derives and runs all 22 exact projection-mode replacements, comparing both spellings after only receipt/volatile metadata removal. The corpus caught --collapse <value> and health --check-only as independent execution semantics; both are excluded from false replacement mapping and --collapse now emits truthful weaker guidance. Remaining scope before this general feature can close: derive and execute the other forward-reference kinds, declare the full obligation set as assurance data, and add the cross-kind negative-control gate."
  "2026-08-13T22:27:26.637Z","harness:codex","Assurance evidence: tracker-context-quality initially blocked because the new executable migration spec was test-command linked but not file-owned. Added explicit project file ownership; preserved the pre-existing one-path orphan ceiling rather than weakening the ratchet."
  "2026-08-13T23:17:37.958Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence for this PR tranche: derived and executed all 22 replacement promises across list/search/get/health/deps/graph/history/activity/validate/events/contracts in a real temporary tracker; exact legacy-versus-canonical projections match after removing only invocation receipts and volatile run metadata. Linked PM tests passed 20/20. Full repository coverage passed 7,280 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. Packed npm acceptance exercised canonical CLI normalization and the public SDK, with independent npx and bunx dispatch succeeding. The broader feature remains open for the other forward-reference kinds and its cross-kind assurance negative control."
  "2026-08-13T23:21:03.759Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1005 at implementation commit a4b33ccb3. The PR combines executable migration contracts, nested budget receipts, token-gate correction, generated SDK/contracts/changelog artifacts, and all-status GitHub/PM lineage."
  "2026-08-13T23:53:26.657Z","harness:codex","PR #1005 exact implementation head 079303e2e passed every hosted deterministic gate, including aggregate exact coverage, Codecov patch, static quality, typecheck, compatibility, smokes, Windows, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, and benchmarks. No inline review threads exist. CodeRabbit and Sourcery were explicitly quota-limited and hosted Greptile produced no response surface; these are provider limitations, not approvals. This executable recovery tranche is delivered for review while the broader feature remains open for cross-kind forward-reference and assurance-negative-control continuation."
  "2026-08-14T11:04:49.120Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-14: recovery references in this tranche will become executable across CLI, SDK, and MCP, with positive replay and invalid/stale cursor negative controls rather than prose-only promises."
  "2026-08-14T12:39:42.839Z","harness:codex","Executable-recovery evidence: bounded output now publishes one recovery.cursor plus declared CLI, SDK, and MCP bindings; the real temporary list-closed acceptance walks every page through the emitted value and rejects malformed, stale, and cross-command cursors. The broader cross-kind forward-reference corpus remains residual."
  "2026-08-14T12:57:50.456Z","harness:codex","Tranche closeout: this PR executes the new bounded cursor recovery through the real CLI and verifies malformed/stale/cross-command failures, extending the forward-reference corpus beyond migration hints. The general feature remains open because other emitted recovery/next-step kinds and the cross-kind assurance pass-fraction gate are not yet complete."
  "2026-08-14T19:13:55.121Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-14: derive the remaining forward-reference vocabulary from typed contracts, execute command-path and recovery obligations in isolated workspaces, expose coverage as assurance data, and add a negative control that proves a broken reference blocks."
  "2026-08-14T20:29:42.511Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence 2026-08-14: the SDK now models suggested_retry, candidate_command, example, and next_step obligations with per-kind coverage and stable findings. The integration corpus executes a real emitted retry in an isolated tracker, validates six candidate paths against the live unbounded command contract, and records 10/10 reachability; a seeded broken reference reduces pass_fraction to 0.9 and blocks repository-context-quality. All four linked test commands passed. The broader feature remains active through PR review; full generator-derived coverage of every emitted reference family remains the honest residual."
  "2026-08-14T20:32:24.595Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1015 — typed cross-kind recovery reachability with executable retry/path proof and assurance enforcement."
  "2026-08-14T20:52:19.046Z","harness:codex","Review implementation: recovery-reference assurance now rejects duplicate obligation ids without allowing one observation to discharge multiple promises; integration validation requires complete declared candidate command paths and no longer accepts arbitrary subcommands through root-only matching."
  "2026-08-14T21:13:10.802Z","harness:codex","Review verification: the full repository suite passed 495 files and 7,309 tests at exact 100% coverage: 53,181 statements, 39,226 branches, 10,929 functions, and 51,358 lines. The executable repository-context gate passed all four provider assertions, including recovery-reference coverage; token surface passed 79 surfaces."
  "2026-08-14T21:59:24.877Z","harness:codex","Review evidence for PR #1015 exact-head amendment: recovery-reference pass_fraction now divides by unique declared ids while duplicate obligations remain fail-closed; mixed duplicate-plus-valid proof asserts the 0.5 receipt; real-entrypoint expectations derive kind counts and negative-control ratios from emitted obligations. Verification: focused recovery tests passed and full repository coverage passed 7,313 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; provider-backed context gate passed 4 assertions and the 79-surface token gate passed."
  "2026-08-14T23:07:08.995Z","harness:codex","Merged delivery evidence: PR #1015 merged exact reviewed head 0939a5a51 as main commit 5f3e4c809. The shipped SDK corpus covers suggested_retry, candidate_command, example, and next_step with 10/10 current reachability, full command-path validation, duplicate-obligation protection, unique-id pass fractions, and a blocking negative control. Exact repository coverage, static gates, CI, security, telemetry, and Sentry all pass. Residual acceptance remains: the obligation corpus is not yet generated from every producer table for every emitted reference family, and replacement-versus-behavior-preserving execution is not yet unified across the full cross-kind set. Returning it open and unclaimed rather than overstating completion."
  "2026-08-15T14:34:45.931Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-15: unify producer-derived recovery obligations with executable replacement and behavior-preserving contracts across CLI, SDK, and MCP, then ratchet them through native assurance."
  "2026-08-15T15:05:16.763Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: recovery obligations are now derived recursively from emitted envelopes and generated read-output alias contracts rather than handwritten test rows. Coverage includes suggested_retry, candidate_command, example, next_step, migration_hint, and restore_with with enforced recovery/replacement/behavior_preserving semantics; real temporary-tracker tests execute representative retry, replacement, preservation, and unbounded restoration paths plus a broken-reference negative control."
  "2026-08-15T15:42:12.339Z","harness:codex","Disposable packed-consumer acceptance 2026-08-15: installed package CLI and SDK paths exercised the complete-read recovery and explicit bounded-omission contract through npm/npx and Bun/bunx. Producer-derived recovery tests separately execute retry, candidate path, replacement, behavior-preserving, and restore_with semantics against temporary trackers."
  "2026-08-15T16:20:30.156Z","harness:codex","Tranche closeout 2026-08-15: the implementation now derives suggested_retry, candidate_command, example, next_step, migration_hint, and restore_with obligations recursively from emitted envelopes and read-output alias producers, declares recovery/replacement/behavior_preserving semantics, executes real temporary-tracker paths, and fails a seeded broken reference. All four linked commands and the exact 7,387-test 100/100/100/100 suite pass. Honest residual: this is not yet a complete census of every forward-reference producer table and emitted product envelope, so the feature remains open and will be released rather than closed."
  "2026-08-15T16:32:09.254Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1035 at exact implementation head 7a5653524a38b69099730a5bf8cf7a58e271db6b. Hosted checks and bot review are in progress; merge and release evidence will be appended separately."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T22:07:15.884Z","harness:codex","A migration flag can belong to a universal output dimension without being replaceable by the universal option. Promise strength must be explicit contract data: parsing a well-formed hint or checking that its target flag exists cannot distinguish projection equivalence from preserved traversal, grouping, side-effect, cursor, or streaming semantics."
